[line]
[size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]Description[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Kiln is a mod framework and launcher for Enshrouded, in the spirit of Forge. One app installs Kiln into your game, manages your mods and runs your servers. Mods work in the game client and on dedicated servers, including Linux.

Mods are written in C#, with JSON for data. Kiln also loads mods made for other Enshrouded frameworks (EML, ShroudForge, EMF, Enshwick, Greeneye and more) without rewriting them. Each adapter has its own limits; check the compatibility guides for the mods and loader combination you use.[/color][/size]

[quote][size=3][b][color=#F9C74F]Safe by default[/color][/b]
[color=#D4D4D8]On a game build Kiln doesn't know, its hooks and C# mods stay off and the game runs as normal. Uninstalling restores the files it replaced.[/color][/size][/quote]

[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Learn more in the [url=https://frostdev.io/kiln/wiki][color=#F9C74F]wiki[/color][/url]. Kiln is free and open source under the MIT licence: the code is on [url=https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kiln][color=#F9C74F]GitHub[/color][/url]. Its EML and ShroudForge parts are GPL-3, like the projects they are built from, and their source comes with every release.[/color][/size]

[size=2][color=#A1A1AA]Kiln is unofficial and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Keen Games.[/color][/size]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]Runs mods for other frameworks[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]0.2.0-dev.28:[/b] Kiln loads these frameworks' mods next to Kiln mods. You don't need a separate framework install where Kiln supplies its runtime. Drop the mod on the launcher window (zip, 7z, rar, folder or DLL), or put it where its framework puts it: the launcher lists the mods it finds in the game folder and says whether they load. Many changes in this release were checked only under Wine and on lab servers, not on a real client. Server and host checks do not guarantee every mod pairing or player-facing feature; the wiki lists the evidence and remaining game checks.[/color][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]EML (Enshrouded Mod Loader):[/b] data mods run with EML's own code before the game starts. No dbghelp.dll and no Wine setting needed. Installed by default. Starts read far less game data: on a lab server under Wine, checking the game files for a start that changed nothing took 64 ms instead of 5.4 s. A first start no longer reads all game files (about 48 GiB on a full install), and a small window shows progress when the step before the game takes longer than two seconds. Kiln restores or replaces only game data it can prove it wrote; files it cannot prove are moved aside (kiln/eml/displaced in the game folder) and named in the launcher, never deleted. [color=#A1A1AA]Untested in game; start speed not measured on a real client.[/color][/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]ShroudForge:[/b] Kiln ships its runtime (1.7.9), with asset publication and recovery fixes; or use your own installed ShroudForge in Settings. Installed by default. Each ShroudForge mod has a page in Kiln's in-game menu and in the launcher with its switch, settings and buttons, and mod shortcuts work without ShroudForge installed. ShroudForge 1.8.0 will be supported when it is released. [color=#A1A1AA]Mixed server startups with EMF Lua and Beastmaster passed; joined gameplay, the in-game page and shortcuts still need game checks.[/color][/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]EMF[/b] 0.3.3 through 0.6.8 / API v40: DLL and Lua mods, EMF's own Lua mods among them (Beastmaster, Necromancer, Bounty Board and the others). Installed by default. Radial wheels, right-click window events, health/stamina/mana access and mod messaging are implemented, and a Kiln game answers an EMF server's mod check. [color=#A1A1AA]Limits:[/color] most of what EMF added since 0.6.0 answers "not available" for now (player events, buffs, markers, map actions, canvases and more: the wiki lists them); programs and event listeners stay in the server's world. Wheel input, custom portraits, taming and joined multiplayer still need game checks.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]SET (Shrouded Engine Tweaks):[/b] Lua mods for SET 0.2 and older, also on dedicated servers, with rules, saved mod settings, level/flame administration, text lookup and Kiln tool windows. [color=#A1A1AA]Limits:[/color] game options, Admin.send, ImGui Debug and SET's settings.ini editor remain unavailable, and the tool windows are not all of SET's own overlay; window drawing and input need a client check.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Greeneye Loader:[/b] The Worst Map Mod, Find, Quick Deposit and more, also on Linux and Steam Deck. Each mod runs from its own folder in the game (greeneye/<mod>), where it keeps its settings. [color=#A1A1AA]Untested in game.[/color][/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Creative Mode (Flame):[/b] runs without its loader. [color=#A1A1AA]Untested in game.[/color][/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Shroudtopia:[/b] minimaps and older tweaks. [color=#A1A1AA]Untested in game.[/color][/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Enshwick:[/b] DLL, Luau and data-pack mods. Kiln ships Enshwick's own loader; a copy you installed still wins. [color=#A1A1AA]Untested in game.[/color][/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]shroudlink:[/b] server mods (chestsort, assistants, storage, meter, gemforge) without the steam_api64.dll proxy. shroudlink's client addon, when you install it, always loads before Kiln hooks the game. [color=#A1A1AA]Works on a test server; untested with players, and its MODS tab is not yet confirmed in a real game.[/color][/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Ember:[/b] mods are found and listed, but don't run until Ember publishes its loader.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Stand-alone dinput8.dll mods:[/b] Kiln keeps them and loads them next to itself. Closed-source DLL mods such as XHL-Core can load after Kiln: turn on [b]Load after Kiln and ShroudForge[/b] for the entry under [b]Load order[/b], Native and DLLs, which also shows hook overlaps from the last session with a one-click [b]Load late[/b]. A DLL listed twice loads once. [color=#A1A1AA]Not yet checked on a real client.[/color][/color][/size][/*]
[/list]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Your other loader is installed too?[/b] Kiln keeps the files it replaces and detects active framework loaders so its own adapter can step aside. While such a loader is installed, the launcher copies your mods of that framework into the folder it reads, so they load whichever loader runs. Use one startup owner for each framework: late-loaded native loaders and competing hooks can still conflict. A mod folder you changed in the game folder is never replaced or removed: the launcher tells you that it stayed and whether it may still run. Uninstalling restores the files Kiln replaced. Details and limits: [url=https://frostdev.io/kiln/wiki/other-mods][color=#F9C74F]Mods for other frameworks[/color][/url] in the wiki.[/color][/size]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]Installation instructions[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]Install Kiln[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Download the Kiln Launcher[/b] for your system from the Files tab when available, or the frostdev.io / GitHub links above: the Windows installer, or the AppImage or .deb on Linux.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Open the launcher.[/b] It finds Enshrouded in your Steam libraries by itself. If it doesn't, use Add a folder.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Press Install Kiln[/b] on the Play page and confirm. Everything Kiln needs comes with the launcher.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Press Play.[/b] Steam's Play button also starts Kiln from now on, with the mods you switched on.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]


[quote][size=3][b][color=#F9C74F]Nexus downloads in 0.2.0-dev.28[/color][/b]
[color=#D4D4D8]The launcher's Nexus Catalog, account sign-in and Mod Manager Download (nxm) links are disabled while OAuth approval is pending. Use Manual Download in your browser, then drop the mod archive on the launcher or use Add mods on the main screen. Personal API keys are not a fallback. If 0.2.0-dev.19 took over nxm links, this build gives them back to your previous handler (Vortex, for example). [color=#A1A1AA]Not yet checked on a Windows PC.[/color] The launcher distributed here on Nexus has no self-updater; download new launcher versions manually.[/color][/size][/quote]

[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]Add mods[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Drop the mod's zip, 7z, rar, folder or DLL onto the launcher window.[/b] It appears in the list on the main screen, switched on, whether it's a Kiln mod or a mod for another framework. Every mod there has an on/off switch. Undo takes it out again.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Press [b]Play[/b]. Your saves are backed up first when your mod list has changed, a mod that brings its own models, animations or sounds is prepared ("cooked") from your game's files, and the launcher shows what the start is doing until the main menu.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]More than one set of mods? In [b]Settings[/b], save the current set as a profile and load another there. A mod's menu in the list lets you pick between the versions you added.[/color][/size]


[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]Linux (Proton)[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]GE-Proton 11-11 needs no launch options. Older builds need this in Steam's launch options, and the launcher tells you when:[/color][/size]
[code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="dinput8=n,b" %command%[/code]

[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]Steam Deck[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]On a Steam Deck the launcher opens in a controller-friendly mode. Download the AppImage in Desktop Mode and right-click it, [b]Add to Steam[/b], to start it from Game Mode. [b]Add mods[/b] lists the mods in your Downloads folder, and [b]Help[/b] shows the one Steam setting.[/color][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]Dedicated servers[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Rented server with only FTP or a file manager, or your own Windows PC: download the optional file [b]Kiln server pack[/b] (kiln-server-<version>.zip) and unzip it into the server folder, the one with enshrouded_server.exe. It includes the server parts for EML, ShroudForge, EMF and the other frameworks. KILN-SERVER-README.txt inside has the steps. Own Linux server without a desktop: [b]kilnctl[/b] from [b]Kiln runtime (manual install)[/b] installs and runs it under Wine. Then check kiln/logs/kiln.log for "boot complete". Players need Kiln only for mods that say so. The full guide is in the [url=https://frostdev.io/kiln/wiki][color=#F9C74F]wiki[/color][/url]. Windows servers have been tested under Wine so far, not yet on a real Windows PC.[/color][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]Uninstall[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Use Uninstall on the Runtime page. It restores the original files and keeps your saves.[/color][/size]
[line]
[size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]Main features[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]The launcher[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Runtime:[/b] install, update, roll back and uninstall Kiln[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]One list of all your mods:[/b] every mod of every framework on the main screen with an on/off switch; profiles in Settings for several sets of mods[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Several mods at once:[/b] select mods in the list and switch them on, off or remove them in one go; All on and All off, with Undo[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]A start you can follow:[/b] Play shows a progress bar with the step that runs and, from the second start, the time left[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Per mod:[/b] its settings, its versions and one-click Remove in the row's menu; a Load order view of every mod; imports mods for every framework Kiln runs; Remove and Clean up are refused while Enshrouded runs[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Steam Deck mode:[/b] the whole launcher with a controller, starts by itself on a Deck[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]One-off starts:[/b] play vanilla or without mods, for one session only[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Your files stay yours:[/b] a mod folder or game file that Kiln did not write, or that you changed, is left alone and named, with what may still run from it[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Saves:[/b] backups and restore, plus a built-in save editor, also on the Steam Deck[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Data folder:[/b] move everything Kiln keeps (mods, runtimes, modpacks, profiles, backups) to another folder or drive, in Settings, Library. Tested by the launcher's own tests, not yet on a Windows PC[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Mod updates:[/b] Check for updates tells you when a mod has a newer version and links its page; nothing is downloaded behind your back, and the daily check is off until you switch it on[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Logs:[/b] game and mod logs and crash reports in one place, and a support report in one zip with names and paths removed[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]


[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]Servers[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Run from the launcher:[/b] install and run dedicated servers, with the console built in and no extra window[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Admin pages:[/b] players, live map, zones, items, spawning, world, combat, creatures, permissions, configs, mods, saves and crashes[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Modpacks:[/b] publish one for your server. Players who are missing mods get an offer to install it, with their consent and hash checks[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]


[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]What mods can do[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Game data:[/b] change recipes, loot, stack sizes, item stats, spells and skills, and values the game reads once at its start (how many Flame Altars a base may have, the experience each level needs), from the very first start[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Gear:[/b] add items, weapons, armor and recipes, with names in each language, icons and 3D models; weapons can have attacks and animations of their own, and a mod can keep data on one single item and roll bonuses onto it[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Creatures:[/b] add your own, with their own level, scale and spawning[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Abilities and talents:[/b] add abilities, extend the talent tree or add whole new trees[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Quests and NPCs:[/b] add quest chains, friendly NPCs, dialogue and voice acting, shown in the game's own journal, NPC menu and map[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Sounds:[/b] add and replace them[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]World:[/b] build structures and change terrain, add ore veins, mounds and tunnels that never overwrite your own building. Players without Kiln see these too[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Rules and admin tools:[/b] flight and NoClip for a player, kick and ban, the weather[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Interface:[/b] add screens and menu entries in the game's own style, and their own numbers and bars in the item details, slots and HUD; the pause menu scrolls when mods add many entries, and key bindings take the mouse wheel and side buttons[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]


[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]For mod authors[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Start with the [url=https://frostdev.io/kiln/wiki/first-mod][color=#F9C74F]first mod guide[/color][/url] in the wiki.[/color][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]C# on .NET 10:[/b] hot reload, events, configs, commands and dependencies between mods[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]SDK:[/b] packages, 32 project templates and the kiln command line tool; use the matching 0.2.0-dev.28 MDK for this release[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Checks:[/b] analyzers, a linter for mod files, and a searchable catalog of game data built from your own install[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]VS Code extension:[/b] completion, hover, build, deploy and a debugger[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Tests:[/b] run them inside a live server, or offline with dotnet test[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]


[size=4][b][color=#F9C74F]Works with other mods[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Runs mods for [b]EML, ShroudForge, EMF, SET, Greeneye Loader, Creative Mode, Shroudtopia, Enshwick and shroudlink[/b], unchanged (see above)[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Loads [b]plain DLL mods[/b][/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]If another tool already uses dinput8.dll, Kiln keeps it and loads it. Other loaders stay installed; Kiln steps aside when they run[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]One hook registry:[/b] Kiln's own hooks and the hooks of EMF and Shroudtopia mods share one detour per game function, and kiln/state/hooks.json lists them with any other DLL's hook Kiln finds. [color=#A1A1AA]Checked under Wine and on lab servers, not yet on a real client.[/color][/color][/size][/*]
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b][color=#FF6A1A]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Game:[/b] Enshrouded on Steam, or the Enshrouded dedicated server[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]System:[/b] Windows 10 or 11, Steam Deck, or Linux with Proton (glibc 2.35 or newer: Ubuntu 22.04 and later, Fedora, Mint, Debian 12, Arch)[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Nothing else:[/b] Kiln brings its own private .NET runtime, and the Windows installer sets up WebView2 if it's missing[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]


[quote][size=3][b][color=#F9C74F]Good to know[/color][/b]
[/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Game updates.[/b] Mods stay off until a Kiln update supports the new build. The game itself keeps working.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Multiplayer.[/b] A server whose mods need Kiln refuses players without it. Players with Kiln who lack a required mod are refused too, and told which mods are missing. That check covers Kiln mods; mods for other frameworks (EML data mods above all) must match the server too, and a server's modpack can carry them.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Playing vanilla.[/b] A character carrying items from a Kiln mod can crash on a server that lets players without Kiln in, and may lose those items elsewhere. Use another character.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8][b]Removing a mod.[/b] It can remove that mod's items from your characters and worlds. The launcher backs up your saves before a start with a changed mod list.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]
[/quote]
[line]
